IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 5 TELECOMMUNICATION CABLE DETECTION WORK: ss 33 to 36.
-- Seat: the person who digs (earthworks near a telecommunication cable), the cable detection worker, and the telecommunication system licensee.
-- 2000 Revised Edition numbers: s 33 was s 29, s 34 was s 30, s 35 was s 31, s 36 was s 32.  The licensing regulations are Rg 4
-- (sgta-i-rg4-cable.l4).

§ `s 33 Telecommunication cable detection work to be carried out before earthworks`

-- src:2583 | 33.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person must not commence or
-- src:2584 | carry out, or cause or permit the commencement or carrying out of,
-- src:2585 | any earthworks which are within the vicinity of any
-- src:2586 | telecommunication cable belonging to or under the management or
-- src:2587 | control of a telecommunication system licensee unless —
-- src:2589 | (a) the person has given to the telecommunication system
-- src:2590 | licensee at least 7 days’ (or such other period as the
-- src:2591 | Authority may allow in any particular case) notice in
-- src:2592 | writing of the date on which it is proposed to commence
-- src:2593 | the earthworks;
-- src:2595 | (b) the person has obtained from the telecommunication
-- src:2596 | system licensee the necessary information on the
-- src:2597 | location of such telecommunication cable and has
-- src:2598 | consulted the licensee on the steps to be taken to prevent
-- src:2599 | the telecommunication cable from damage while the
-- src:2600 | earthworks are being carried out; and
-- src:2602 | (c) the person has caused telecommunication cable detection
-- src:2603 | work to be performed or carried out by a licensed
-- src:2604 | telecommunication cable detection worker in order to
-- src:2605 | confirm the location of the telecommunication cable.
@ref s 33(1) (src:2583-2605)
GIVEN `the earthworks are within the vicinity of a telecommunication cable belonging to or under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of notice in writing given to the licensee of the date proposed to commence the earthworks, or the period the Authority allowed in the particular case` IS A NUMBER
      `the Authority allowed another period for notice in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtained from the licensee the necessary information on the location of the cable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person consulted the licensee on the steps to be taken to prevent the cable from damage while the earthworks are carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person caused telecommunication cable detection work to be performed by a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker to confirm the location of the cable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(1): the person may commence or carry out, or cause or permit, the earthworks` MEANS
    (NOT `the earthworks are within the vicinity of a telecommunication cable belonging to or under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee`)
    OR (    (`the Authority allowed another period for notice in the particular case` OR (`days of notice in writing given to the licensee of the date proposed to commence the earthworks, or the period the Authority allowed in the particular case` AT LEAST 7))
        AND `the person obtained from the licensee the necessary information on the location of the cable`
        AND `the person consulted the licensee on the steps to be taken to prevent the cable from damage while the earthworks are carried out`
        AND `the person caused telecommunication cable detection work to be performed by a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker to confirm the location of the cable`)

-- src:2607 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prohibit a person from commencing or
-- src:2608 | carrying out any earthworks where the person has reasonable cause to
-- src:2609 | believe that it is necessary to do so in the interest of public or private
-- src:2610 | safety, except that the person must, not more than 7 days after the
-- src:2611 | earthworks have been commenced or carried out, give to the
-- src:2612 | telecommunication system licensee a written notice stating the
-- src:2613 | nature and extent of those earthworks.
@ref s 33(2) (src:2607-2613)
GIVEN `the person has reasonable cause to believe that it is necessary to commence or carry out the earthworks in the interest of public or private safety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after the earthworks were commenced or carried out that the person gave the licensee a written notice stating the nature and extent of the earthworks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(2): subsection (1) does not prohibit the person from commencing or carrying out the earthworks` MEANS
    `the person has reasonable cause to believe that it is necessary to commence or carry out the earthworks in the interest of public or private safety` AND (`days after the earthworks were commenced or carried out that the person gave the licensee a written notice stating the nature and extent of the earthworks` AT MOST 7)

-- src:2618 | (3) It is the duty of the person who carries out any earthworks
-- src:2619 | referred to in subsection (1) —
-- src:2621 | (a) to comply with all reasonable requirements of the
-- src:2622 | telecommunication system licensee for the prevention of
-- src:2623 | damage to the telecommunication cable;
-- src:2625 | (b) to ensure that reasonable precautions are taken when
-- src:2626 | carrying out such earthworks to prevent any damage to the
-- src:2627 | telecommunication cable, including but not limited to site
-- src:2628 | supervision of the earthworks; and
-- src:2630 | (c) to allow the telecommunication system licensee reasonable
-- src:2631 | access to the work site for the purpose of inspecting or
-- src:2632 | taking any necessary measures to protect the
-- src:2633 | telecommunication cable.
@ref s 33(3) (src:2618-2633)
GIVEN `the person complied with all reasonable requirements of the licensee for the prevention of damage to the cable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ensured that reasonable precautions were taken, including site supervision, to prevent damage to the cable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person allowed the licensee reasonable access to the work site for inspecting or taking necessary measures to protect the cable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(3): the person has discharged the duty` MEANS
    `the person complied with all reasonable requirements of the licensee for the prevention of damage to the cable` AND `the person ensured that reasonable precautions were taken, including site supervision, to prevent damage to the cable` AND `the person allowed the licensee reasonable access to the work site for inspecting or taking necessary measures to protect the cable`

-- src:2635 | (4) It is the duty of a telecommunication system licensee to whom a
-- src:2636 | notice under subsection (1)(a) has been given —
-- src:2638 | (a) to promptly inform the person who has given the
-- src:2639 | telecommunication system licensee the notice of the
-- src:2640 | location of the telecommunication cable and to provide
-- src:2641 | such person with any other information as may be
-- src:2642 | necessary to enable the person to ascertain the exact
-- src:2643 | location of the telecommunication cable;
-- src:2645 | (b) to advise the person who has given the telecommunication
-- src:2646 | system licensee the notice on the precautions to be taken to
-- src:2647 | prevent damage to the telecommunication cable; and
-- src:2649 | (c) to take all such measures at the work site as may be
-- src:2650 | reasonable and necessary for the protection of the
-- src:2651 | telecommunication cable from damage and, in so doing,
-- src:2652 | the telecommunication system licensee must have regard
-- src:2653 | to the potential risks and dangers that can arise from any
-- src:2654 | damage to the telecommunication cable.
@ref s 33(4) (src:2635-2654)
GIVEN `the licensee promptly informed the person who gave the notice of the location of the cable and provided other information necessary to ascertain its exact location` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee advised the person who gave the notice on the precautions to be taken to prevent damage to the cable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee took all measures at the work site that are reasonable and necessary for the protection of the cable, having regard to the potential risks and dangers from damage to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(4): the telecommunication system licensee has discharged the duty` MEANS
    `the licensee promptly informed the person who gave the notice of the location of the cable and provided other information necessary to ascertain its exact location` AND `the licensee advised the person who gave the notice on the precautions to be taken to prevent damage to the cable` AND `the licensee took all measures at the work site that are reasonable and necessary for the protection of the cable, having regard to the potential risks and dangers from damage to it`

-- src:2656 | (5) A person (other than a licensed telecommunication cable
-- src:2657 | detection worker) must not commence or carry out any
-- src:2658 | telecommunication cable detection work within the vicinity of any
-- src:2659 | telecommunication cable belonging to or under the management or
-- src:2660 | control of a telecommunication system licensee where such
-- src:2662 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2663 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 54
-- src:2665 | telecommunication cable detection work is commenced or carried out
-- src:2666 | in connection or combination with or in relation to any earthworks
-- src:2667 | carried out or to be carried out.
@ref s 33(5) (src:2656-2667)
GIVEN `the person is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person commences or carries out telecommunication cable detection work within the vicinity of a telecommunication cable belonging to or under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is carried out in connection or combination with, or in relation to, earthworks carried out or to be carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(5): the person has contravened the prohibition` MEANS
    (NOT `the person is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker`) AND `the person commences or carries out telecommunication cable detection work within the vicinity of a telecommunication cable belonging to or under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee` AND `the work is carried out in connection or combination with, or in relation to, earthworks carried out or to be carried out`

-- src:2669 | (6) Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with
-- src:2670 | subsection (1) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:2671 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000 or to
-- src:2672 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
@ref s 33(6) (src:2669-2672)
GIVEN `the person contravenes or fails to comply with subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 33(6): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person contravenes or fails to comply with subsection (1) or (3)` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 100000, 36, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2674 | (7) Subject to subsection (8), in any proceedings for an offence
-- src:2675 | under subsection (6), it is a defence for the person charged to prove —
-- src:2677 | (a) that the person took all reasonable steps to discharge the
-- src:2678 | person’s duty under subsection (1) or (3), as the case may
-- src:2679 | be; or
-- src:2681 | (b) that the person took all reasonable precautions and
-- src:2682 | exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of
-- src:2683 | the offence.
@ref s 33(7) (src:2674-2683)
GIVEN `the person proves that the person took all reasonable steps to discharge the person's duty under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(7): the person charged has a defence to the offence under subsection (6)` MEANS
    `the person proves that the person took all reasonable steps to discharge the person's duty under subsection (1) or (3)` OR `the person proves that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`

-- src:2685 | (8) If in any proceedings for an offence under subsection (6) the
-- src:2686 | defence involves acting on information supplied by a
-- src:2687 | telecommunication system licensee or a licensed
-- src:2688 | telecommunication cable detection worker, the person charged is
-- src:2689 | not, without permission of the court, entitled to rely on that defence
-- src:2690 | unless, within 14 clear days before the hearing, the person charged
-- src:2691 | has served on the prosecutor a written notice giving such information
-- src:2692 | as was then in the person’s possession identifying or assisting in the
-- src:2693 | identification of the person who supplied the information to the
-- src:2694 | person charged.
@ref s 33(8) (src:2685-2694)
GIVEN `the defence involves acting on information supplied by a telecommunication system licensee or a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the person who supplied the information was served on the prosecutor within 14 clear days before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 33(8): the person charged may rely on the defence` MEANS
    (NOT `the defence involves acting on information supplied by a telecommunication system licensee or a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker`) OR `a written notice identifying or assisting in the identification of the person who supplied the information was served on the prosecutor within 14 clear days before the hearing` OR `the court gave permission`

-- src:2698 | (9) Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with
-- src:2699 | subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:2700 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:2701 | term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 33(9) (src:2698-2701)
GIVEN `the person contravenes or fails to comply with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 33(9): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person contravenes or fails to comply with subsection (5)` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 10000, 12, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `ss 34 to 36`

-- src:2711 | 34. The Authority may —
-- src:2713 | (a) grant a telecommunication cable detection work licence
-- src:2714 | permitting a person to perform such telecommunication
-- src:2715 | cable detection work as is specified in the licence and may
-- src:2716 | suspend, cancel, alter, extend, renew or replace any such
-- src:2717 | licence;
-- src:2719 | (b) classify any telecommunication cable detection work
-- src:2720 | licence in such manner as it determines;
-- src:2722 | (c) specify the nature of the telecommunication cable
-- src:2723 | detection work in respect of which a telecommunication
-- src:2724 | cable detection work licence is granted and restrict such
-- src:2725 | work to any type or class of telecommunication cable
-- src:2726 | detection work;
-- src:2728 | (d) specify the circumstances or manner in which licensed
-- src:2729 | cable detection workers may perform or carry out
-- src:2730 | telecommunication cable detection work;
-- src:2732 | (e) impose any terms, conditions or restrictions on any
-- src:2733 | telecommunication cable detection work licence;
-- src:2735 | (f) require any public telecommunication licensee to conduct
-- src:2736 | approved courses of training, including refresher courses,
-- src:2737 | and provide for examinations for telecommunication cable
-- src:2738 | detection workers;
-- src:2740 | (g) keep a register of licensed telecommunication cable
-- src:2741 | detection workers; and
-- src:2743 | (h) do any act or thing which is necessary or convenient to
-- src:2744 | carrying out the objects of this Part or is incidental thereto.
@ref s 34 (src:2711-2744)
GIVEN act IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34: the Authority may do this` MEANS
    elem act (LIST "grant a telecommunication cable detection work licence permitting a person to perform the telecommunication cable detection work specified in it, and suspend, cancel, alter, extend, renew or replace the licence"
                  , "classify any telecommunication cable detection work licence in such manner as it determines"
                  , "specify the nature of the work in respect of which a licence is granted and restrict the work to any type or class of telecommunication cable detection work"
                  , "specify the circumstances or manner in which licensed cable detection workers may perform telecommunication cable detection work"
                  , "impose any terms, conditions or restrictions on any telecommunication cable detection work licence"
                  , "require any public telecommunication licensee to conduct approved courses of training, including refresher courses, and provide for examinations for telecommunication cable detection workers"
                  , "keep a register of licensed telecommunication cable detection workers"
                  , "do any act or thing necessary or convenient to carrying out the objects of this Part or incidental to them")

-- src:2749 | 35.—(1) Any person who, not being a licensed telecommunication
-- src:2750 | cable detection worker, advertises or holds himself or herself out or
-- src:2751 | conducts himself or herself in any way or by any means as a person
-- src:2753 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2754 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 56
-- src:2756 | who is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker shall be
-- src:2757 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:2758 | exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:2759 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 35(1) (src:2749-2759)
GIVEN `the person is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person advertises or holds himself or herself out, or conducts himself or herself in any way or by any means, as a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 35(1): the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the person is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker`) AND `the person advertises or holds himself or herself out, or conducts himself or herself in any way or by any means, as a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 10000, 12, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2763 | (2) A person (other than a licensed telecommunication cable
-- src:2764 | detection worker) is not entitled to recover in any court any charge,
-- src:2765 | fee or remuneration for any telecommunication cable detection work
-- src:2766 | performed or carried out by the person.
@ref s 35(2) (src:2763-2766)
GIVEN `the person is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(2): the person is entitled to recover in court a charge, fee or remuneration for telecommunication cable detection work performed` MEANS
    `the person is a licensed telecommunication cable detection worker`

-- src:2772 | 36. Any person who digs, bores, trenches, grades, excavates or
-- src:2773 | breaks any ground with any mechanical equipment or explosive or
-- src:2774 | allows employee or agent of the person to do so without first
-- src:2775 | ascertaining the location of any telecommunication cable belonging
-- src:2776 | to or under the management or control of any telecommunication
-- src:2777 | system licensee that may be interfered with shall be guilty of an
-- src:2778 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2779 | $100,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to
-- src:2780 | both.
@ref s 36 (src:2772-2780)
GIVEN `the person digs, bores, trenches, grades, excavates or breaks ground with mechanical equipment or explosive, or allows an employee or agent to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person first ascertained the location of any telecommunication cable of a telecommunication system licensee that may be interfered with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty`
`s 36: the person is guilty of an offence and the most the penalty may be` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the person digs, bores, trenches, grades, excavates or breaks ground with mechanical equipment or explosive, or allows an employee or agent to do so` AND (NOT `the person first ascertained the location of any telecommunication cable of a telecommunication system licensee that may be interfered with`) THEN JUST (`Penalty` OF 100000, 36, 0, FALSE)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
